# ETK RADIO -- the debrief rung (spec 4, layer 1).
#
#   ollama create etk-radio:9b -f tools/radio/Modelfile.debrief
#
# qwen3.5:9b is the credentialed analyst rung (docs/RADIO_CREDENTIAL.md, spec 10.3):
# richer and more precise than the 4b on mechanism, at ~40% more wall clock. Async,
# toasted when ready, so the wall clock is affordable; the 4b (Modelfile.fast) is the
# interactive radio-check rung and the legitimate single-model fallback.
#
# NO `SYSTEM` LINE HERE, DELIBERATELY. The doctrine (prompts/engineer.md) is sent by the
# service as the system message of every call, and `prompt_sha256` in the debrief is
# hashed over exactly the bytes that were sent. Baking the doctrine into the model would
# make that hash a lie -- the debrief would claim a prompt the model never received as a
# message -- and it would put a corpus refresh (`git -C ~/etk pull`) out of step with the
# model until someone remembered to re-run `ollama create`. Sending it every call costs
# nothing: it is the same bytes each time, so Ollama's prefix cache carries it (82-118
# tok/s cached vs 17.9 cold on this node, spec 10.2), which is the whole reason the
# doctrine is FIRST in the prompt and the per-pack briefing is last.
#
# THINKING IS OFF. Ollama's Modelfile has no `think` directive, so it cannot be set here:
# the service passes `"think": false` in the /api/chat body (tools/radio/exam.py does the
# same, and falls back to omitting the key if the endpoint rejects it). Deliberate --
# a 4B spent 2,766 tokens deliberating over a two-sentence question on this node, and
# generation is the budget: 630 output tokens is ten minutes on the 9b.
#
# The service still sends `options` explicitly on every call (num_ctx from
# briefing.build()'s `num_ctx`, which rises to 16384 when the prompt needs it) and
# `format:` = tools/radio/schema/debrief.v1.json for constrained decoding. These
# PARAMETER lines are the floor, not the contract -- they make `ollama run etk-radio:9b`
# behave the same way by hand as it does through the service.

FROM qwen3.5:9b

# Near-deterministic. This is forensics, not prose: the same pack should read the same way
# twice, and the eval re-runs cases across seeds to check that it does.
PARAMETER temperature 0.2

# The doctrine (~1.5k) + briefing + pack fit inside 8192 by construction: briefing.py
# refuses to build over 4,500 prompt tokens (spec 12 -- every 1,000 tokens of evidence is
# a minute on the 9b), and the never-truncate guard rejects a pack that would not fit
# rather than letting Ollama silently decide what the model saw.
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192

# Generation cap. A debrief is a headline, a radio line, a few findings and a run sheet;
# ~300 tokens in practice. 700 is the ceiling that keeps a runaway answer from costing
# the operator ten minutes of wall clock.
PARAMETER num_predict 700
